sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Team as Project Migration Team
    participant SN as ServiceNow (CMDB)
    participant GH as GitHub Actions Runner
    participant EV as EventBridge Scheduler
    participant DR as Drift Reconciler
    participant PG as Policy/Approval Gate
    participant TF as Terraform/Config Enforcer
    participant DB as Database Drift Controller
    participant AWS_SSM as AWS Systems Manager
    participant EC2 as Temporary Builder EC2

    %% Phase 1: Intake & Governance
    Team->>SN: Submit Catalog Migration Request
    Note over SN: Approvals complete.<br>Create/Update CMDB CI Configuration.
    SN->>GH: Trigger Workflow via REST Webhook (Repository Dispatch)<br>[Payload: AppID, Middleware Type, Env, ChangeID]

    %% Phase 2: Orchestration & Checkout
    activate GH
    GH->>GH: Execute Git Checkout (App Code + Ansible Roles)
    Note over GH: If Java (Tomcat/WebLogic):<br>Compile Source to .WAR / .EAR via Maven
    GH->>AWS_SSM: Assume IAM Role via OIDC (Fetch Temp Security Token)
    GH->>GH: Initialize Ansible Controller Runtime & Install AWS SSM Session Manager Plugin

    %% Phase 3: Cloud Execution via SSM Session Manager
    GH->>GH: Trigger Ansible Image Build Playbook
    activate AWS_SSM
    GH->>AWS_SSM: Ansible launches EC2 in Private Subnet (No Public IP/No Port 22 Open) via amazon.aws module
    Note over GH, EC2: Ansible communicates over encrypted SSM Session Manager tunnel<br>(no SSH required)
    GH->>EC2: Push Application Artifacts & Ansible Playbooks across SSM Tunnel

    %% Phase 4: Inner-Loop Configuration Management
    activate EC2
    Note over EC2: Local Ansible execution starts:<br>1. Hardens Base OS<br>2. Sets up selected Middleware (Tomcat/WebLogic/Python)<br>3. Injects Application Artifacts
    EC2-->>GH: Streaming Logs / Success Code
    deactivate EC2

    %% Phase 5: Image Serialization & CMDB Loopback
    GH->>AWS_SSM: Ansible stops instance & registers new Golden AMI via amazon.aws modules
    GH->>AWS_SSM: Ansible terminates Temporary Builder Instance
    AWS_SSM-->>GH: Return New AMI ID (e.g., ami-01234abcd)
    deactivate AWS_SSM

    GH->>SN: Send API Patch Request:<br>Update CMDB CI with New Active AMI ID + Ansible execution references
    Note over SN: CMDB and Change Record are updated with<br>AMI + Ansible execution evidence for audit tracking

    %% Phase 6: Continuous Drift Detection and Closed-Loop Remediation
    EV->>DR: Scheduled reconciliation trigger
    DR->>DR: Compare live AWS configuration<br/>vs Git/Terraform desired state
    DR->>SN: Publish drift findings and evidence
    DR->>PG: Raise remediation decision request
    alt Policy allows auto-remediation
        PG->>TF: Authorize enforce baseline execution
        TF->>TF: Run Terraform apply/config re-run<br/>to match repository baseline
    else Manual approval required
        PG->>Team: Request approval for controlled remediation
        Team->>PG: Approve remediation
        PG->>TF: Authorize enforce baseline execution
        TF->>TF: Run Terraform apply/config re-run<br/>to match repository baseline
    end
    TF->>DR: Return post-remediation state
    DR->>DR: Verify convergence to desired baseline
    DR->>SN: Update CMDB/compliance status with closure evidence

    %% Phase 7: Dedicated Database Drift Detection and Remediation
    EV->>DB: Scheduled database drift control trigger
    DB->>DB: Detect schema/config drift against versioned migration baseline
    alt DB drift detected
        DB->>PG: Request migration remediation decision
        PG->>DB: Approve migration execution policy
        DB->>DB: Execute migration orchestration
        alt Migration validation fails
            DB->>DB: Execute rollback (snapshot restore/previous migration)
        end
        DB->>DB: Perform post-remediation validation
        DB->>SN: Publish DB drift status and remediation evidence
    else No DB drift
        DB->>SN: Record compliant DB baseline state
    end
    deactivate GH
